# The Pixhawk settings the companion stack relies on, for the team airframe.
# Load in Mission Planner (Config > Full Parameter List > Load from file)
# AFTER aerothon_failsafe.parm, then reboot. Copter 4.5.
#
# Without these the stack's MAVLink commands are accepted and do nothing:
# camera_ctrl's MAV_CMD_DO_MOUNT_CONTROL needs a mount on the camera servo's
# output, and MAVROS needs the port it is wired to.
#
# CHANNELS ARE WIRING (operator, 24 Oct 2026): the webcam tilt servo is on
# SERVO5 (MAIN OUT 5). The payload motor is driven by the Pi (BTS7960/H-bridge
# on Pi GPIO, winch_ctrl backend:=gpio), so the FC has no winch output.

# Companion link: Pi 5 UART0 (GPIO14/15) at 115200, MAVLink 2. Set the FC
# port the Pi is wired to: SERIALn_PROTOCOL 2 and SERIALn_BAUD 115 for that
# port. Not set here -- the port number is wiring, and a wrong baud here
# would cut the link that works.

# Camera tilt: a hobby servo on SERVO5 whose pulse width the Pi sets with
# MAV_CMD_DO_SET_SERVO (operator, 27 Oct 2026; camera_ctrl fc_output servo).
# No mount, and the output must be free: only the Pi drives it (operator,
# 29 Oct 2026). A passthrough takes it back from the Pi whenever its channel
# moves past RCn_DZ (56, RC6, the winch switch, did; 58, RC8, did until
# 29 Oct). Receiver channel 8 tilts the camera through the Pi instead
# (camera_ctrl rc_tilt_channel 8), so RC8 must do nothing here: RC8_OPTION 0.
# GCS Camera cal records the pulse width for forward, 45 deg and straight down.
MNT1_TYPE 0
SERVO5_FUNCTION 0
# The former camera output is released.
SERVO9_FUNCTION 0

# Winch: the Pi drives the payload motor directly; no FC winch.
WINCH_TYPE 0
SERVO10_FUNCTION 0

# RC channel 6, a three-position switch, commands the payload motor by hand
# when no autonomous mission runs (winch_ctrl rc_manual_channel 6, read through
# rc_in_bridge on /aerothon/rc/in). Channel 6 must do nothing on the FC: keep
# RC6_OPTION 0 and TUNE 0 (in-flight tuning knob), and FLTMODE_CH off 6 (this
# aircraft, 25 Oct 2026: FLTMODE_CH 7; channel 5 is a two-position switch).
